# Fixed defect 133, 2026-09-29. Symptom: `enum Color` with no cases cost
# `reserved_word` alone, and only once `check --apply` had written
# `variant Color` did the next run report `empty_variant`; a case field
# missing its colon under `union` waited the same way. Cause: the lexer
# emits the refused word as an `error` token, and at a top-level line's head
# the parser's recovery dropped the whole declaration with its cases. The
# parser now reads `enum` and `union`, whose certain swap is `variant`, as
# `variant` (`parse/swap_reading.hero`). An empty `variant` is refused at
# the next line's first token, as it is after the swap, so the one under
# `enum Color` lands on the `union` line.
#
# Moved the same day, a second round (defect 131's class): `empty_variant`
# points at its own head now, `enum Color`, as `empty_record` does, and no
# longer at the next line's first token, a line the author did nothing wrong
# on.

variant Ok
    yes
    no

variant Color  #~ reserved_word empty_variant

variant Shape  #~ reserved_word
    circle
        r f64  #~ expected_field_type
    square

variant Suit  #~ reserved_word
    hearts
    spades

function main()
    print(1)
